  "help": {
    "title": "Help",
    "subtitle": "Frequently asked questions about the platform.",
    "q1": "How to watch live channels?",
    "a1": "Navigate to the 'Channels' section from the main menu. Select the channel you want to watch and playback will start automatically. Channels with the red indicator are broadcasting live.",
    "q2": "How to add content to favorites?",
    "a2": "On the detail page of any movie, series, or channel, tap the heart icon to add it to your favorites. You can view all your favorites from the 'Favorites' section in the menu.",
    "q3": "What is the EPG Guide?",
    "a3": "The EPG (Electronic Program Guide) shows the TV programming schedule. You can see what's currently airing and future programming, filtered by day.",
    "q4": "Video doesn't load or stops",
    "a4": "Check your internet connection. If the problem persists, try a different channel or content. Some streams may be temporarily unavailable. If nothing works, contact the server administrator.",
    "q5": "How to change my password?",
    "a5": "Go to 'Settings' by clicking your username in the top bar. In the 'Change Password' section, enter your current password and the new one. The new password must be at least 8 characters long.",
    "q6": "How does history work?",
    "a6": "Your playback history is saved automatically. When you stop watching a movie or episode, the progress is saved. Next time you visit, you can continue from where you left off in the 'Continue Watching' section.",
    "q7": "What video formats does the platform support?",
    "a7": "The platform supports HLS (HTTP Live Streaming) playback and direct video file playback. Local content is automatically transcoded to the appropriate format."
  },
